# Local Dev CSS Cache

**Policy:** Default local dev uses **webpack**, not Turbopack, so `globals.css` HMR stays in sync with JSX.

## Why

Turbopack (`next dev --turbopack`) can serve **stale CSS** from `.next` while component HTML updates via HMR. Production builds are always fresh; localhost may look wrong until cache is cleared.

## Commands

| Script | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `npm run dev` | Normal dev (**webpack** — preferred) |
| `npm run dev:turbo` | Faster dev when not editing global CSS |
| `npm run dev:clean` | Styles still wrong after `globals.css` changes — deletes `.next` then starts webpack dev |

## After editing `globals.css`

1. Save the file; webpack dev should hot-reload CSS.
2. If localhost still shows old styles: stop dev, run `npm run dev:clean`, hard-refresh browser (`Cmd+Shift+R`).
3. Verify in DevTools that the expected rule exists in the loaded CSS bundle.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] After `globals.css` typography/layout changes, remind user to hard-refresh if verifying locally
- [ ] Do not assume localhost matches production if only Turbopack dev was running with a stale `.next`
- [ ] Prefer `npm run dev` (webpack) over `dev:turbo` when changing global styles
